Z||000008||fiero56||04-13-2000||09:33 PM||||I think what he means is the problem is not an aluminum clutch pedal not allowing proper disengagement of the clutch. With bent clutch pedals, it is normal to be able to shift through the gears with the engine off, but when the engine is running it is very diffucult to shift through the gears, and avoid grinding the gears due to improper clearnances.<P>It means the clutch is bad.||||reg||1
